hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"367","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ishaq ibn 'Isa Abu Hisham narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from 'Abd Rabbihi ibn al-Hakam, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of Ta'if, some slaves belonging to them came out to him and embraced Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them. When their masters later embraced Islam, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the wala' (clientage) to them."
"368","Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Hassan — narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The inheritance of a people is not to be fragmented when it cannot bear division."
"369","Muhammad ibn 'Awf narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ka'b narrated to us, 'Isa narrated to us, from Thawr, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nusayr, the freed slave of Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the division that causes harm."
